==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-au-give the time of day.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[give]] (somebody ''or'' someone) the [[time]] of [[day]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[acknowledge]] somebody; to give somebody respect or attention.
#: ''If you're lucky, she might '''give you the time of day'''.''
#: ''Unless you're a celebrity, he won't '''give you the time of day'''.''
# {{lb|en|literal}} {{lb|en|dated}} To tell someone the time of day by looking at one's [[wristwatch]], etc.

====Usage notes====
* '''Give somebody the time of day''' is usually used in the [[negative]].

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|not give someone the time of day}}

